./working_notes/claim_ledger.md:82:## Claim: Worst-action \(\Delta_T(H)=o(T)\) is necessary for sublinear regret
./working_notes/claim_ledger.md:86:Evidence: Horizon \(T\): set \(P_1=\cdots=P_{T-1}=0\), \(P_T\sim\mathrm{Unif}[0,1]\). A law-aware learner quotes \(1/2\) every early round and gets zero regret, but for \(H=o(T)\) most comparator rewards arrive only at \(T\), so \(\Delta_T(H)\approx (T-H)/4=\Omega(T)\).
./working_notes/claim_ledger.md:241:Dependencies: Horizon \(T=D+1\); unknown class with two exogenous worlds; learner is not told the active world; \(P_1=\cdots=P_D=0\); terminal distribution is \((1-q)\delta_0+q\,{\rm Unif}[1/2,5/8]\) in world \(L\), and \((1-q)\delta_0+q\,{\rm Unif}[3/4,7/8]\) in world \(H\). For raw \(\beta\) claims, extend after \(T\) with absorbing prices \(P_s=0\).
