./iterations/iter_007/idea_02/idea.md:1:# Rare-History Beta Separation
./iterations/iter_007/idea_02/idea.md:6:Formalize the solver's rare-history example: draw N with P(N=n)=c 4^{-n}, reveal a symbol s_N at time 1, then run L_N=2^n zeros followed by one spike at 1. Prove beta(h)=1 for every h, but Delta_T(H) is O(1/H) uniformly in T and the comparator value is bounded.
