./logs/iter_006_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:1240:Facts needed: Essential supremum over histories can keep \(\beta(H)\) large, while \(\Delta_T(H)/T\) remains small because the histories almost never occur.
./logs/iter_006_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:1241:Why it matters: Would show strict weakness of average truncation criteria compared with \(\beta\).
./logs/iter_006_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:1245:## Tiny-price long-delay blocks may break raw beta without meaningful regret
./logs/iter_006_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:1247:Facts needed: For every \(h\), some block creates a conditional state with \(\Pr(h<\tau<\infty)=1\), so \(\beta(h)=1\). But if \(p_m\) decreases fast enough, total best fixed comparator value may be \(o(T)\), making sublinear regret trivial.
