./iterations/iter_006/idea_02/explorer_01.md:3:The tiny-price block idea works. It gives a deterministic singleton process with \(\beta(h)=1\) for every \(h\), while the best fixed-quote value is uniformly bounded over all horizons. Thus the zero-quote learner has \(O(1)\) regret. This is a clean counterexample to raw delay-probability necessity.
