./logs/iter_002_synthesis.stderr.log:7402: ## Claim: Worst-action \(\Delta_T(H)=o(T)\) is necessary for sublinear regret
./logs/iter_002_synthesis.stderr.log:7432: Facts: For each early quote, expected reward is \(a(1-a)\), maximized at \(a=1/2\). The learner can quote \(1/2\) and get zero regret. For any \(H=o(T)\), most early rewards are excluded by truncation, so \(\Delta_T(H)\approx (T-H)/4=\Omega(T)\).
./logs/iter_002_synthesis.stderr.log:7455: ## Original "only if beta" conjecture
