./logs/iter_005_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:830:Failure: False under law-aware/process-wise quantifiers. For iid uniform prices, \(\beta(h)=1\) for all \(h\), but a learner knowing the law can play the best fixed quote in expectation and get zero regret. Iteration 2 strengthened this: for every finite-horizon known exogenous law, a horizon-aware conditional grid oracle gets regret at most \(T/K\).
