./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:856:## Claim: Worst-action \(\Delta_T(H)=o(T)\) is necessary for sublinear regret
./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:860:Evidence: Horizon \(T\): set \(P_1=\cdots=P_{T-1}=0\), \(P_T\sim\mathrm{Unif}[0,1]\). A law-aware learner quotes \(1/2\) every early round and gets zero regret, but for \(H=o(T)\) most comparator rewards arrive only at \(T\), so \(\Delta_T(H)\approx (T-H)/4=\Omega(T)\).
./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:900:Dependencies: Horizon \(T=D+1\); unknown class with two exogenous worlds; learner is not told the active world; \(P_1=\cdots=P_D=0\); terminal distribution is \((1-q)\delta_0+q\,{\rm Unif}[1/2,5/8]\) in world \(L\), and \((1-q)\delta_0+q\,{\rm Unif}[3/4,7/8]\) in world \(H\). For raw \(\beta\) claims, extend after \(T\) with absorbing prices \(P_s=0\).
./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:906:Scaling by \(q\) gives Bayes gap \(q/8\) per unresolved quote round, hence some world has regret at least \(qD/8\). With absorbing extension, \(\beta(h)=q\) for \(h<D\) and \(0\) for \(h\ge D\). For integer \(H<D\),
./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:930:## Claim: Raw \(\beta\) may fail because of rare histories while average truncation succeeds
./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:934:Evidence: Essential sup can be driven by histories of tiny unconditional probability, while \(\Delta_T(H)/T\) averages over realized histories.
./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:938:## Claim: Raw \(\beta\) may fail because long delayed hits have tiny value
./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:942:Evidence: Long zero blocks followed by prices \(p_m\downarrow0\) can keep \(\beta(h)=1\) along arbitrarily long gaps, while attainable comparator value may remain \(o(T)\).
./logs/iter_004_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:1024:## 3. Write the clean sufficient theorem with \(\delta_T(H)\)
