./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:1487:./logs/iter_002_solver.stderr.log:402:## Claim: Worst-action \(\Delta_T(H)=o(T)\) is necessary for sublinear regret
./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:1489:./logs/iter_002_solver.stderr.log:406:Evidence: Horizon \(T\): set \(P_1=\cdots=P_{T-1}=0\), \(P_T\sim\mathrm{Unif}[0,1]\). A law-aware learner quotes \(1/2\) every early round and gets zero regret, but for \(H=o(T)\) most comparator rewards arrive only at \(T\), so \(\Delta_T(H)\approx (T-H)/4=\Omega(T)\).
./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:1497:./logs/iter_002_solver.stderr.log:434:Evidence: Essential sup can be driven by histories of tiny unconditional probability, while \(\Delta_T(H)/T\) averages over realized histories.
