./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:1683:./iterations/iter_001/idea_01/idea.md:6:Turn the solver's Delta_T(H) truncation into a precise theorem for a process class C: for any H,K there is a grid delayed-full-information learner with sup_{P in C} R_T(P) <= C sqrt(T H log K)+T/K+sup_{P in C} Delta_T^P(H), where Delta_T^P(H)=sup_a sum_t E[r_t(a)-r_t^H(a)]. Then derive exact qualitative condition: existence of H_T,K_T with H_T log K_T=o(T), T/K_T=o(T), and uniform Delta_T(H_T)=o(T).
