./logs/iter_002_idea_01_explorer_01.stderr.log:2081:./logs/iter_002_solver.stdout.log:5:The original “sublinear regret iff \(\beta(h)\to0\)” is false. Under a law-aware exogenous model, no tail condition is needed at all. Under a uniform/minimax-over-unknown-class model, the clean upper bound is known, and the hidden-terminal construction gives a real lower-bound mechanism, but I do not yet have a full necessary-and-sufficient characterization.
