./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:564:## Claim: Worst-action \(\Delta_T(H)=o(T)\) is necessary for sublinear regret
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:568:Evidence: Horizon \(T\): set \(P_1=\cdots=P_{T-1}=0\), \(P_T\sim\mathrm{Unif}[0,1]\). A law-aware learner quotes \(1/2\) every early round and gets zero regret, but for \(H=o(T)\) most comparator rewards arrive only at \(T\), so \(\Delta_T(H)\approx (T-H)/4=\Omega(T)\).
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:592:## Claim: Raw \(\beta\) may fail because of rare histories while average truncation succeeds
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:596:Evidence: Essential sup can be driven by histories of tiny unconditional probability, while \(\Delta_T(H)/T\) averages over realized histories.
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:600:## Claim: Raw \(\beta\) may fail because long delayed hits have tiny value
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:604:Evidence: Long zero blocks followed by prices \(p_m\downarrow0\) can keep \(\beta(h)=1\) along arbitrarily long gaps, while attainable comparator value may remain \(o(T)\).
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:611:## Original "only if beta" conjecture
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:612:Attempt: Prove that sublinear regret is possible only if the essential-sup hitting tail \(\beta(h)\to0\).
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:613:Failure: False under law-aware/process-wise quantifiers. For iid uniform prices, \(\beta(h)=1\) for all \(h\), but a learner knowing the law can play the best fixed quote in expectation and get zero regret. Iteration 2 strengthened this: for every finite-horizon known exogenous law, a horizon-aware conditional grid oracle gets regret at most \(T/K\).
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:619:Failure: The conditional grid oracle gives \(R_T\le T/K\) for every such law. With \(K=T\), regret is \(O(1)\) independent of \(\beta\), \(\Delta\), or \(\delta\).
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:623:## Treating \(\Delta_T(H)=o(T)\) as a characterization
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:624:Attempt: Replace \(\beta\) by the average/worst-action truncation loss \(\Delta_T(H)\) and claim necessity.
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:625:Failure: Singleton terminal-spike law has zero law-aware regret but \(\Delta_T(H)=\Omega(T)\) for \(H=o(T)\).
./logs/iter_003_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:643:Failure: For fixed \(D\), delay is bounded by \(D\), so asymptotic regret is \(O(D)=o(T)\) and \(\beta(h)=0\) for \(h\ge D\).
